            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0333" n="221" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg221"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 4002/266.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1909-12-06"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 6, 1909</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1313.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of my No. 1292, of the 14th
                    ultimo, on the subject of the municipal administration of Harbin, I have the
                    honor to inclose a copy in translation of a note from Prince Ching inclosing a
                    copy of a circular identic note addressed by the Wai-wu Pu to the
                    representatives of the powers in Peking on the subject of the interpretation of
                    the agreement (1896) for the construction of the Chinese Eastern Railway. This
                    circular note was adduced by the aide-mémoire of the Russian foreign office of
                    September 23 last, which was communicated to the Chinese Government by the
                    Russian minister. The department will note that the Chinese Government strongly
                    repudiates the Russian contentions and emphatically reasserts Chinese
                    sovereignty in the railway territory.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                    Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>




